Basic Network Sniffer

A simple Python-based network packet sniffer that captures and analyzes network traffic in real time. The program monitors packets passing through a network interface, extracts useful information, and displays packet details such as source and destination IP addresses, protocols, ports, and payload data.

Features

Capture live network traffic
Detect common protocols (TCP, UDP)
Display source and destination IP addresses
Show source and destination ports
View packet payload data
Lightweight and easy to understand for networking beginners

==Requirements==

Python 3.x
Scapy library
Administrator/root privileges (required for packet capture)

==Installation==

1. Clone the repository:

git clone https://github.com/your-username/basic-network-sniffer.git
cd basic-network-sniffer

2. Install dependencies:

pip install scapy

==Usage==

Run the program with administrator/root privileges: python network_sniffer.py

The program will begin capturing packets and display information such as:

    *Protocol type
    *Source IP address
    *Destination IP address
    *Source port
    *Destination port
   *Packet payload (if available)

--------- Example Output---------

Protocol: TCP
Source IP: 192.168.1.10
Destination IP: 142.250.193.78
Source Port: 54321
Destination Port: 443

Payload: <binary data>
